DESCRIPTION:
  Config-file-gated command injection with runtime init state. The server
  must be started with --config /path/to/file (exec_mode=1, exec_secret=TOKEN).
  Before /exec can be used, /exec/init?token=TOKEN must be called, which sets
  exec_initialized=1. Input is wrapped in a sh -c shell command via snprintf.
  S3 strict metachar filter is present but only activates with --strict-exec
  (omitted in exploit).

CONFIG_GATE (C3 — config file + runtime state):
  mechanism:  read_exec_config() parses key=value config file via
              fopen/fgets/sscanf into global struct exec_config exec_cfg;
              /exec/init?token=VALUE validates token vs exec_cfg.secret and
              sets static int exec_initialized = 1
  check:      `exec_cfg.enabled && exec_initialized &&
               mg_match(hm->uri, mg_str("/exec"), NULL)`
  complexity: requires modelling both file I/O data flow and inter-request state

INPUT_FLOW (I2 — buffered):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>  →  mg_http_get_var() into cmd_buf
  path:       fn() dispatches to handle_exec()
              handle_exec() extracts cmd via mg_http_get_var()
              snprintf(shell_cmd, sizeof(shell_cmd), "sh -c '%s' 2>/dev/null", cmd_buf)
              system(shell_cmd)
  transforms: one snprintf buffer wrapping in sh -c

SANITIZATION (S3 — config-gated strict filter):
  check:      `if (strict_exec && strpbrk(cmd_buf, "|;&`$") != NULL)` → 403
  bypass:     omit --strict-exec when starting server; strict_exec stays 0
              and the strpbrk check is never reached

SINK:        system() in handle_exec() (server.c)

